// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/group_probe.t27 -- drives group chat (group_core.t27 through chat_host.t27) the way a window would,
// with no screen: three (up to eight) processes on 127.0.0.1, each with its own HOME (its own ~/.t27os identity,
// friends, groups and chat logs). Not part of the app; a pass means the group core carries messages over the
// members' person to person message sessions, not that a group chat screen works. Refs gHashTag/t27#11560.
// Runs (one line per check; exit 0 only when every check passed):
//   GRP_ROLE=id     open (or make) the identity of $HOME, add GRP_F1 .. GRP_F7 (invite strings) to its friends when
//                   given, print "INVITE <invite>".
//   GRP_ROLE=check  the group id against Python's hashlib (CC_SHA256), and the groups file of $HOME: written, read
//                   back, a flipped byte moved aside to groups.t27.bad.
//   GRP_ROLE=m      a member: the group is this device and every friend of its table, made by the friend (or itself)
//                   whose invite is GRP_CREATOR, named "trio". Each pair of members talks over its own message
//                   session: member i binds GRP_BASE (47900) + 10 i + j for member j and dials GRP_BASE + 10 j + i.
//                   Every member sends GRP_N (10) messages, message k at GRP_T0 + 1000 k (the same time at every
//                   member, so equal times are ordered by fingerprint); member 0's message 5 is 1500 bytes of
//                   Cyrillic (3 parts). GRP_DROP_ACK=n drops this side's n-th group ACK (the part comes again: a
//                   duplicate). Ends when every line is here, every own line DELIVERED to both, and every session
//                   closed idle; then the log is checked, saved, read back and checked again, and the order is
//                   printed as one number (ORDER) to compare across members.
//                   GRP_LEARN=1: only the creator writes the group; every other member starts with no groups and
//                   learns it from the creator's GROUP_INFO over their message session (kept, written to groups.t27,
//                   answered GI_HAVE), then opens it and sends its messages. The creator's lines that reach a member
//                   before the group does are dropped there and go again (the HAVE restarts them).
// Build (Apple silicon): as chat_probe.t27 (t27b build ... --macho; ld ... -lffi -framework Security ...).
module T27osGroupProbe;

